<header class="ref-head"><span class="hero-ornament"></span><h1 class="research-title">17 June in history</h1><p class="ref-lede">6 events that happened on 17 June, from 1462 to 1994.</p></header>
<ol class="day-events"><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb tih-event-hero"><p class="tih-hero-kicker">&#10022; Anniversary of the day</p><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/vlad-the-impaler" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/vlad-the-impaler.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1462">1462 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">564 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Vlad the Impaler attacks the Ottoman camp by night</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Vlad III of Wallachia led a night raid on <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sultan">Sultan</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mehmed-ii">Mehmed II</a>'s camp near Târgovişte, failing to kill the sultan. His reputation for cruelty later fed the legend behind Bram Stoker's Dracula.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag tih-tag-profile" href="/empire/ottoman-empire">Ottoman Empire</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mehmed-ii">Mehmed II</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1579">1579 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">447 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Francis Drake claims Nova Albion for Elizabeth I</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">During his circumnavigation, Drake landed on the coast of what is now northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/california">California</a> and claimed it for <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/england">England</a> as Nova Albion. England made no attempt to settle it.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/england">England</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1775">1775 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">251 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">British take Breed's Hill at heavy cost in the Battle of Bunker Hill</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">After two failed assaults, British troops drove colonial militia from the heights near <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/boston">Boston</a>. They suffered more than 1,000 casualties, proving the Americans could stand against regulars.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/boston">Boston</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1944">1944 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">82 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Iceland becomes a republic</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">At <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/thingvellir">Þingvellir</a>, the site of its ancient assembly, Iceland ended its union with the Danish crown and proclaimed a republic. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/denmark">Denmark</a> was then under German occupation.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/denmark">Denmark</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1972">1972 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">54 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Five men are arrested in the Watergate building</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Burglars linked to President Nixon's re-election committee were caught inside the Democratic National Committee offices in Washington. The cover-up led to Nixon's resignation in 1974.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1994">1994 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">32 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">O. J. Simpson leads police on a televised chase</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">About 95 million viewers watched police follow a white Ford Bronco carrying the former football star along <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/los-angeles">Los Angeles</a> freeways. Simpson was later acquitted of murdering his ex-wife and her friend.</p></div></li></ol>
